 "note": "International Trading Company Store (former), 83 Bussell Hwy, Margaret River's third store (1925), later the Margaret River Art Gallery and Jahroc, REDSEA Gallery since 2024 (local heritage list MR(T)-04). From the inHerit record and a 2019 street photo; footprint NOT measured (placement unconfirmed). A single-storey timber weatherboard shop, dark oiled timber, with a gabled Zincalume roof to the street, a modern bull-nosed verandah over the footpath, a splayed central entry between big timber-framed shop windows, the 2005 flat-roofed contemporary gallery (black, deep red fascia) beside it, and the old cottage behind (outbuilding). Name in plain lettering. Metres: x left to right as seen from Bussell Hwy (north to south), y back (east) from the shopfront.",
